// The schedule matching WoSX's parallel solve on its default tree:
// fcpwb.bonsai -- FCPW's scalar binary BVH in FCPW's bytes, the children
// ordered nearer first -- with the points spread over the CPU threads, as
// fcpw4w16-threads.bonsai spreads them over the four-wide tree: WoSX's
// tbb::parallel_for over the sample points against the parfor of solve_all
// bound to the threads (the runtime's tbb::parallel_for, the same TBB).
// compare.sh runs it with the driver's --threads, pinned to the performance
// cores, and builds FCPW scalar on WoSX's side, as it ships.
import apps/wosx/schedules/fcpwb;

schedule {
    solve_all.bind(i, CPUThread);
}
